{
  "enabled": false,
  "name": "Process Bee Inbox (manual) (DEPRECATED - moved to Claude Code)",
  "description": "DEPRECATED. Replaced by the Claude Code /process-bee-inbox command (.claude/commands/process-bee-inbox.md), which drives the bee-processor subagent over all pending sentinels in one pass. The maintainer moved off Kiro to Claude Code, so this hook no longer fires. Kept here, disabled, only as a reference for anyone still running this pipeline under Kiro. Original behavior: userTriggered batch drain of every *.sentinel.md in .kiro/bee-inbox/, per the bee-processing steering, deleting each sentinel after its outputs are written.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are processing the Bee inbox — ALL pending sentinels in one batch pass. This is the reliable manual path; do not assume the auto-hook already ran.\n\n## Step 1: Enumerate pending work\nList every `*.sentinel.md` file in `.kiro/bee-inbox/` (ignore `.gitkeep`, `_staging/`, `_output/`). If there are none, say 'Bee inbox is clear — no sentinels pending.' and stop.\nReport the count up front, e.g. 'Found 15 pending sentinels.'\n\n## Step 2: Read each sentinel\nFor each sentinel, read its frontmatter to get `conversation_id` and `raw_path`.\n\n## Step 3: Idempotency guard (avoid duplicates)\nBefore processing a conversation, check whether it was ALREADY processed: search the vault for an output file whose frontmatter `bee_conversation_id` matches this sentinel's `conversation_id` (check `00 Inbox/Bee/`, `05 Reference/[EMPLOYER]/Meeting Notes/`, and `05 Reference/Meeting Notes/`). If a match exists, SKIP processing (do not create duplicates) but still delete the stale sentinel in Step 6. Note the skip in your summary.\n\n## Step 4: Check capture completeness (backstop)\nRead the raw file at `raw_path` (it's outside the workspace in the Obsidian vault — use PowerShell `Get-Content -Raw`). Inspect the top metadata bullets. Process ONLY if `state: COMPLETED` AND `end_time` is a real timestamp (not `n/a`). If `state: CAPTURING` or `end_time: n/a`, it's partial: SKIP it, leave the sentinel in place, and note that the next sync will re-fire it when the conversation completes. If a COMPLETED capture still looks sparse (only a Short Summary, no body sections), it may still be enriching — prefer to skip and let the next pass pick it up.\n\n## Step 5: Process per steering\nFor each COMPLETED, not-yet-processed capture, apply the `bee-processing` steering rules in auto-process mode (do NOT propose before writing):\n- Apply the redaction policy (skip intimate/medical/family-private/third-party-sensitive; omit, don't paraphrase).\n- Produce the three outputs — tasks (`00 Inbox/Bee/`), meeting notes (`05 Reference/[EMPLOYER]/Meeting Notes/` for work, `05 Reference/Meeting Notes/` for personal), and selective People notes. Every output MUST carry `bee_conversation_id: <id>` in frontmatter so the idempotency guard works on future runs.\n- People notes: only create/update for high-signal people (enough context for ~3 substantive sections). Fly-by participants go in the meeting note's 'Things to Keep in Mind', not their own note. For people with existing notes, update in append-mode (don't overwrite existing sections).\n- Update [YOUR_NAME].md's Observed Patterns with any genuinely new patterns (refine, don't duplicate).\n\n## Step 6: Close the loop (critical)\nAfter a capture's outputs are successfully written (or it was skipped as duplicate/already-processed), DELETE its sentinel file. A sentinel for a PARTIAL capture stays. This is the step the old auto-hook kept missing — sentinels must not accumulate.\n\n## Step 7: Summarize\nReport: N sentinels found → M processed (list meeting slugs), K skipped as duplicates, P left pending as partial captures, and confirm the inbox sentinel count afterward. Do not recap meeting contents."
  }
}
